course: dictionary
lesson: 4607
title: Hibernate and other winter words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have two meanings, and the context tells you which one to use. «Hedgehogs feed up in autumn, then hibernate in a nest of leaves» is about animals. Hibernate means to spend the winter in a deep, sleep-like state, with the body slowed down to save energy.
explain: Context also tells you what a word does. «If you find a hibernating animal, do not wake it.» The sentence tells you not to wake it, so the animal is in a deep sleep that is hard to break. Ask yourself: what would happen if I did?
explain: The same word can work in a new place. «Mum says her laptop is hibernating.» A laptop cannot sleep like a hedgehog, so hibernate must mean something else here: it has switched to a power-saving state and keeps your work safe. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence.
fact: Hibernate is a verb. Hibernates, hibernated and hibernating are its other forms.
fact: «Hibernate» means to spend the winter in a deep sleep-like state, with the body slowed down, to save energy.
fact: Animals that hibernate include hedgehogs, dormice, bats, some squirrels and frogs.
fact: «Bears go into a lighter winter sleep»: that is not full hibernation.
fact: For a computer, «hibernate» means to switch to a power-saving state that keeps your work.
exercise: «Some animals hibernate: they go into a deep sleep in a sheltered place.» What does hibernate mean? | *Spend the winter in a deep sleep, saving energy | Swim south across the sea | Build a big nest for the babies | Stay awake all winter, hunting for food
exercise: «Hedgehogs feed up in autumn, then hibernate.» Why do hedgehogs feed up before they hibernate? | To find a new home by the sea | *To store fat to live on during winter | To grow a longer coat | To make their heart beat faster in the cold
exercise: Mum says, «My laptop is hibernating.» What does hibernate mean here? | It has been thrown in the bin | *It has switched to a power-saving state and keeps your work | It has fallen asleep on the sofa
test: «If you find a hibernating animal, do not wake it.» Why is this good advice? | *Waking it uses up the energy it has saved | It will wake up hungry and angry, so it is better to give it food | Hibernating animals enjoy being woken up | A hibernating animal can only be woken by a bear
test: «Bears go into a lighter winter sleep.» What is different about a bear's winter sleep? | It is a deeper sleep than a hedgehog's | It lasts the whole year | It happens only in the summer | *It is lighter than full hibernation
exam: Which of these animals hibernates through winter, according to the lesson? | *Marmot | Robin | Horse | Goldfish
